From 212d0634ab8da72b45f9c2ef2214c67d38cbbefb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kycube <kf1178@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:58:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 30/36] esp32s3.intmatrix: forward a source only when its level
 changes

Since patch 0006 every qemu_set_irq() on a source walks all 99 sources of
both cores to OR the lines routed with it, and sources re-assert unchanged
levels constantly: the GPIO block on every pad refresh, which the panel's
BUSY output triggers once per SPI byte. On the host profile of CrossPoint
page turns (macOS `sample`, 8 turns) the handler was the busiest function,
842 of the 931 samples under epd_transfer(); idle, the USB Serial/JTAG
SOF tick reached it 1000 times a second with the line already low.

The CPU lines are the OR of the sources' levels, so an unchanged level
cannot move them: return early. Re-routing still recomputes both lines
(the map write path is unchanged). The only other effect of a repeated
assertion was to set INTSET again for an edge-type CPU interrupt (10, 22,
28, 30) that the firmware had cleared, which a steady line does not do on
the chip either; ESP-IDF routes the S3's peripherals to level-type
interrupts. Espressif's open PR #185 forwards on change only as well.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 hw/xtensa/esp32s3_intc.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/xtensa/esp32s3_intc.c b/hw/xtensa/esp32s3_intc.c
index 496a5d0..b176950 100644
--- a/hw/xtensa/esp32s3_intc.c
+++ b/hw/xtensa/esp32s3_intc.c
@@ -52,7 +52,14 @@ static void esp32s3_intmatrix_update_output(Esp32s3IntMatrixState *s, int cpu, i
 static void esp32s3_intmatrix_irq_handler(void *opaque, int n, int level)
 {
     Esp32s3IntMatrixState *s = ESP32S3_INTMATRIX(opaque);
-    s->level[n] = level ? 1 : 0;
+    level = level ? 1 : 0;
+    /* Sources re-assert unchanged levels all the time (a GPIO block on every pad
+     * refresh, a peripheral on every register write); the CPU lines are the OR of
+     * the sources' levels, so only a change can move them. */
+    if (s->level[n] == level) {
+        return;
+    }
+    s->level[n] = level;
     for (int i = 0; i < ESP32S3_CPU_COUNT; ++i) {
         esp32s3_intmatrix_update_output(s, i, IRQ_MAP(i, n));
     }
